WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.082
groupby is one of the most important patterns in Pandas.

00:00:04.082 --> 00:00:12.277
Conceptually, it follows three steps: split the rows into groups, apply a calculation to each group,

00:00:12.277 --> 00:00:20.632
and combine the results. In the example, orders are grouped by channel and the amount values are summed.

00:00:20.632 --> 00:00:26.587
The result answers a simple business question: which channel contributes the most revenue?

00:00:27.094 --> 00:00:33.036
Once you understand this pattern, many analyses become easier.

00:00:33.036 --> 00:00:40.711
You can groupby department, city, product, customer segment, month, diagnosis category, or any other meaningful field,

00:00:40.711 --> 00:00:47.324
then calculate counts, totals, averages, minimums, maximums, or other summaries.
